WEBVTT

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:04.340
I don't want to say goodbye

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.470
In order to ride out the winter which had suddenly arrived...

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:10.460
...we said farewell to Everyone's House...

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:12.930
...and moved to a new place.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:16.920
It's been two weeks since then.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:21.390
We've gotten used to our new lifestyle little by little.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:24.780
According to Sharla, our new house...

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.660
...was the crater made by a shooting star.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:28.710
Thus, it was named Star Hole.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.440
Pague!

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:46.310
Pague, healthy?

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.110
Pague, yummy?

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:57.820
Pague!

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:05.570
Eat as much as you can.

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:08.440
He seems to have lost some of his liveliness again.

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:12.200
He doesn't move from here much anymore, after all.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:15.310
But as long as he's here, he's sheltered from the snow...

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:18.150
...and his favourite leaves are here, so he'll be fine.

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:22.710
But the trees around there have few leaves now, for the most part.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.640
When they're gone, all that's left is The Great Tree...

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:28.490
...and when those run out...

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:29.970
That's true...

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:34.930
If he at least had others of his kind, I feel like he might find a way to make it through the winter.

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:39.000
Anyways, I wonder where Pague's family went.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.780
Pague. Pague!

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:49.510
Pague seems happy when he's with Adam.

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.730
It really does seem like this is the cause.

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:05.800
Though we dunno why somethin' like this's comin' out of the ruins.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:07.570
At least we know for sure, though.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:10.500
The sparklin's reflectin' the heat rays.

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:14.030
If we don't stop it somehow, it'll get even colder.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.600
That's why we came, isn't it?

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:21.920
That's the thing you brought out from inside the ruins, right?

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.140
Yep! I'll help too!

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:28.330
Cold!

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:34.000
I think the key to controllin' the ruins is inside the card.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:53.280
We'll connect the card to the communicator and send out a remote control signal.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:57.270
If there's a response, we should be able to open the door.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:04.620
Okay, here I go!

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:18.910
It ain't changin' at all!

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:21.310
Try somethin' or other!

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:27.400
This time!

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:31.050
No good.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:32.130
I'm not done yet!

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:40.810
How about that?

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:49.560
No use...

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:02.660
What's it hope to gain by churnin' out that stuff so fast?

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:05.450
It's a pretty perplexin' machine.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:08.070
There has to be a control device inside.

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:09.270
Damn it!

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:10.750
Open up!

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:11.920
Open up!

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:13.370
Don't make a fool of me!

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:15.450
Why is it making it so cold, though?

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:17.180
I ain't sure.

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:18.920
It's Adam!

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:20.740
He's an alien, after all.

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:23.560
It's making the environment of Adam's planet.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:26.470
Maybe, but Adam's cold too.

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:33.160
Anyways, let's go home and think up another plan of attack.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.220
Everything we can take from this area is gone as well.

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:51.900
It's cold!

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:53.130
I'm sick of this!

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:55.660
Put up with it. Look at Kaoru.

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:05.370
He likes putting up with things.

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:06.940
C'mon, let's dig out the next one.

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:12.720
It really was better looking after Adam.

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:23.430
It's a tributary.

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:24.540
We can't cross this.

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:29.300
Sure can't... We'll have to look for somewhere that's not as wide.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:30.410
I agree.

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:39.840
Pague's kind?

00:07:40.630 --> 00:07:42.290
And a bunch of 'em.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:43.680
Let's check it out.

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:07.780
There were so many of them!

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:10.820
It's an idyllic place, ain't it?

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:12.530
And there's Great Trees.

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:14.950
There's steam comin' off the water.

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.260
It's warm even in winter!

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:28.970
No matter what we did, the door wouldn't move an inch.

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:31.020
We got chilled to the bone trying.

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:34.350
Then you couldn't stop that strange substance from coming out.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:41.100
But what are those ruins, if they're changing the climate?

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:43.260
This was just our guess, but...

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.790
...I think they might be the ruins of a terraforming machine.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:48.560
Terraforming?

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:50.670
What's that?

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:54.480
What they did to the moon we were on!

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:59.580
To put it simply, a machine to change the environment of a planet so people can live there.

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:03.770
Of course I knew that!

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:07.070
I was just testing all of you!

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:08.470
So we passed?

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:10.600
I guess.

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:14.080
But why is a thing like that here?

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:16.960
That's it, this child.

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:21.230
That's right! We can't be sure...

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:26.180
...but maybe the environment Adam lives in is the same as for humans.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:29.320
They're not the same! Look at that cold!

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:35.100
But even on Earth there were many places where it was cold all year round.

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:39.030
I definitely wouldn't want to live in one of those places.

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:40.790
But even so...

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:44.210
...to think that a machine could change the environment so easily...

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:49.250
Somethin' of interest to people aimin' to be Planetary Settlement Engineers.

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:51.020
But...

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:54.010
...there's still one question left about this cold.

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:57.910
Adam was in the ruins, but he's bothered by the cold too.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.420
That's certainly true.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:04.630
What are we going to do if it gets any colder than this?

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:06.540
Will we all just die here?

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:09.050
It's a bit soon to give up.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:12.550
Chako and I will stop that machine somehow!

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:14.800
We're depending on you.

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:18.700
If we can solve the mystery of the ruins, lots of possibilities will open up.

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:19.760
Do whatever you can.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:24.110
Oh, there was one other thing to report on.

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:28.730
On the way back, we found a herd of Pagues.

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:30.380
A herd of Pagues?

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:57.920
There were lots of Pagues bigger than ours gathered together.

00:10:58.230 --> 00:11:01.650
Lots of trees of the same type as The Great Tree were scattered about too.

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:07.400
There was no snow on the ground, and there a green carpet of soft grass.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:12.130
And the pond and river were giving off a warm-looking steam.

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:18.480
All around it was snow, so the place looked just like paradise!

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.530
Then let's move there too!

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:23.500
Our neighbours would be wild animals.

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:25.260
There's no way they'd let us in.

00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:27.450
We'd get trampled underfoot.

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:30.640
You're right. That's a place they found.

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:33.210
I think we'd best let them keep it.

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:38.130
We have a house this warm thanks to Bell and Kaoru.

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:42.320
And however many leaves like The Great Tree's there are...

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:44.600
...it doesn't mean we can eat them.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:47.870
Hey, why don't we take Pague there?

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:52.720
We've laid out hay and protected him from the wind...

00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:54.400
...but he's definitely cold.

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:56.400
And there's not many leaves left.

00:11:57.130 --> 00:11:59.720
Even if you say so, how do you plan to take him there?

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:02.460
We'd have to get him down that cliff.

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:03.800
It's impossible.

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:07.270
But if Pague came from the Eastern Woods...

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:09.630
...shouldn't it be possible to get him back?

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:12.600
Come to think of it, how did Pague get here?

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:14.900
Isn't that obvious?

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:19.430
A bird picked up Pague when he was still a baby.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:22.790
It wouldn't have had a problem getting up a cliff like that.

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:26.300
How about it? Isn't that a logical explanation?

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:27.800
A bird?

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:31.080
There's no bird that big here.

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:35.410
There could be! It'd be like a dinosaur that we haven't seen before.

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:37.290
Flap-flap!

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:41.930
Maybe there's a door!

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:42.760
Door?

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:46.540
One evening under the soft light of a full moon...

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:50.300
...somewhere in the Eastern Woods, a secret door appears.

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:55.520
A door of light forms, connecting it to this forest...

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:59.790
...and a cute baby Pague comes through!

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:01.180
Yeah, yeah!

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:03.410
It's the birth of a new dunce comedian.

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:04.460
What?

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:07.560
That's mean! It was the best I could think of!

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:09.980
Sorry, sorry, I was jokin'.

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.780
Sharla's explanation does have some merit.

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:16.120
Luna?

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:18.270
It might not have been a door...

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:21.120
...but it's possible it was connected by a cave.

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:22.320
I get it!

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:25.110
Once he grew big enough, he couldn't get back through.

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:26.130
Or something.

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:29.240
Anyways, let's look into it tomorrow.

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:33.200
Hey, what will happen to Pague?

00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:37.010
If we can, we'll try to return him to his herd.

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:38.440
Return?

00:13:38.860 --> 00:13:41.680
We're going to show Pague the way back to the Eastern Woods.

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:45.190
He'll go away?

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:50.880
No! I don't want Pague to go away!

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:52.480
Adam...

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:06.400
Even if there is a cave, we don't know if we can use it to get Pague home.

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:10.850
Even if it's not a cave, anywhere we can get Pague home through is fine.

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:16.260
It's true! It's only green here!

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:18.710
It's definitely paradise!

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:23.040
However we have to, I want to bring Pague here.

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:25.910
He may have family in here as well.

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:28.220
He's noticed us!

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:29.620
He's looking this way.

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:31.300
It seems like he's looking at you, Luna.

00:14:32.150 --> 00:14:33.230
I wonder why.

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:38.420
Maybe he caught the scent of Pague left behind on your body.

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:40.670
Then that Pague is...

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:44.370
We have to look for a cave!

00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:52.860
There doesn't seem to be a cave anywhere.

00:14:57.640 --> 00:14:58.640
Maybe a fissure?

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:00.970
It looks like a staircase.

00:15:01.910 --> 00:15:03.450
Maybe he can climb down here.

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:05.640
Here?

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:08.010
Luna! Bell!

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:10.260
What's wrong?

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:14.050
When we took our eyes off him for a moment, Adam disappeared.

00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:16.410
Pague's gone too.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:18.520
We looked, but couldn't find them.

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:20.650
Maybe...

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:31.850
Adam!

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:34.010
Stay away!

00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:35.290
Adam...

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:37.800
You can't just run off like that.

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:39.340
We were worried.

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:41.330
We searched all over for you.

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:42.240
No.

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:44.150
Pague won't go back.

00:15:45.430 --> 00:15:49.820
If we don't return Pague to his herd, he might die of cold.

00:15:49.820 --> 00:15:52.240
No... He'll stay with me.

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:54.120
Don't be so selfish.

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:57.590
Pague might be able to live with his real family.

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:01.810
Pague's parents might be in the herd.

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:05.080
He'd be happier if he could live with his family, wouldn't he?

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:16.820
Let's all help Pague get back to his herd together, okay?

00:16:22.490 --> 00:16:25.050
But Pague is my friend!

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:27.670
I don't want to say goodbye!

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:31.800
Sorry for making you feel sad.

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:36.700
Pague's parents?

00:16:37.950 --> 00:16:40.170
I might just be misinterpreting it, though.

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:45.380
If we can reunite them, I'm sure Pague and his parents would be happy.

00:16:48.660 --> 00:16:51.110
It's impossible to get him down that cliff.

00:16:51.560 --> 00:16:53.760
But it's worth it to try.

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:56.920
If we can get Pague home...

00:16:57.460 --> 00:16:59.510
...we might be able to get home too.

00:17:00.190 --> 00:17:01.110
Don't you think?

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:03.160
I kinda get it.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:06.350
Ridiculous!

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:08.510
Bell, could we use a rope or something?

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:11.610
I've been thinking of using a pulley.

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:12.730
Pulley?

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.620
Coochie-coochie-coo!

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:55.480
It's no use. I'm so hungry I can't move an inch.

00:17:55.870 --> 00:17:58.290
Even if we did this every day, it'd never end.

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:00.660
We're the ones who'll starve to death.

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:03.680
But there's nowhere else to get Pague down.

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:06.180
Yeesh. Let's take a break.

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:08.060
I think I'll go play with Adam.

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:12.620
Coochie-coo. Coochie-coochie-coo. Coochie-coo.

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:14.620
And now, scritch-scritch-scritch-scritch-scritch!

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:18.620
Yeah, scritch-scritch-scritch-scritch, Pague!

00:18:20.170 --> 00:18:21.140
A tobihane?

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:34.410
Howard! It's dangerous!

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:37.370
An avalanche?

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:38.480
Get to high ground!

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:56.060
Everyone! Are you alright?

00:18:57.140 --> 00:18:57.790
That's a relief.

00:18:58.500 --> 00:18:59.270
What about Howard?

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:02.840
Over there!

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:05.160
He wasn't swept away by the avalanche.

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:10.490
Howard, are you hurt?

00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:17.090
You seem fine. That's good.

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:18.030
Luna!

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:20.730
It made a slope!

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:38.050
Everyone, here we go!

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:41.130
Depart!

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:46.190
Hey, Pague...

00:19:46.190 --> 00:19:47.390
What's wrong?

00:19:47.390 --> 00:19:49.080
He's not trying to move.

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:52.450
Maybe Pague don't want to say goodbye neither?

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:01.080
It's the same one as before.

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:03.930
Then maybe it's one of Pague's parents!

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:09.850
Pague, go on.

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:26.130
Slowly, now... Slowly...

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:36.290
Everyone, are you okay?

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:38.280
No problem.

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:40.830
I'll help too.

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:42.060
Adam!

00:20:52.340 --> 00:20:54.660
Just a little further. Keep it up.

00:21:00.550 --> 00:21:07.260
Pague!

00:21:07.380 --> 00:21:08.280
How's Pague?

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:19.900
Pague...

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:22.080
Good for you.

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:32.010
You... did it.

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:34.040
Pague made it home.

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:36.630
We will too...

00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:45.180
Pague went home, but you're not alone, Adam.

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:48.440
We're all your friends and family.

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:55.080
So, should we take in the rope 'n go home?

00:21:56.240 --> 00:21:57.180
What's up, Howard?

00:21:57.480 --> 00:21:58.860
That's not a rope.

00:22:09.630 --> 00:22:12.250
They're sweet potatoes! Full of starch!

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:14.200
There's lots of them!

00:22:14.350 --> 00:22:17.160
They were uncovered when the avalanche moved the snow off them.

00:22:17.580 --> 00:22:19.710
Howard, nice work.

00:22:19.860 --> 00:22:20.650
Nice work...

00:22:21.250 --> 00:22:22.790
Nice... work?

00:22:23.200 --> 00:22:25.110
That's right! It was nice work!

00:22:25.790 --> 00:22:30.850
Making the slope and getting the food were both all thanks to me!

00:22:31.150 --> 00:22:35.540
Of course, since I'm so kind-hearted, I won't keep them all to myself!

00:22:35.690 --> 00:22:38.350
I'll give a little to each of you.

00:22:38.430 --> 00:22:43.110
But in exchange, you'll all call me Lord Howard from now on!

00:22:47.990 --> 00:22:50.200
It's all thanks to Lord Howard!

00:22:50.430 --> 00:22:55.110
--Nobody forget! You should be thanking me!
--Yup, we listened to Lord Howard's bragging...

00:22:55.380 --> 00:22:57.660
...twelve times over.

00:23:04.040 --> 00:23:06.180
Kaoru's past unknown to anyone.

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:09.590
I... killed him.

00:23:11.390 --> 00:23:14.540
What is he hiding in those words?

00:23:15.140 --> 00:23:17.990
Why doesn't he try to come clean with everyone?

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:23.730
Kaoru, what is the burden you carry?

00:23:25.490 --> 00:23:28.150
Next time: In the light
